{%- comment -%}
  Product page (Figma "product pg 1") — portrait image column left, info panel
  right. Every element is a reorderable, hideable block: breadcrumb, title,
  variant picker, description, accordions, media and add to cart. Each piece's
  markup lives once in snippets/pdp-block so nothing drifts.

  TWO COLUMNS, ONE BLOCK LIST: the media block always renders into the left
  column and the gallery into its own grid row, whatever position it holds in
  the list; the rest flow down the info column in block order. Dragging media
  around the list therefore reorders nothing — the layout is a grid, not a
  stack.

  LEGACY FALLBACK: a saved template from before this refactor holds only
  accordion blocks. Rendering it literally would leave a page with nothing but
  two accordions on it, and Shopify validates a template's JSON against the
  schema it had BEFORE the push, so the new block list cannot land in the same
  commit as this file. Until it does, a template with no structural block
  renders the full default order. It costs nothing once the blocks are saved.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product_images = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image'

  assign has_structure = false
  assign media_block = null
  for b in section.blocks
    unless b.type == 'accordion'
      assign has_structure = true
    endunless
    if b.type == 'media'
      assign media_block = b
    endif
  endfor

  assign show_media = true
  if has_structure and media_block == null
    assign show_media = false
  endif

  assign media_ratio = media_block.settings.media_ratio | default: section.settings.media_ratio | default: '4/5'
  assign gallery_gap = media_block.settings.gallery_gap | default: 10
  assign column_gap = section.settings.column_gap | default: 10

  comment
    The media column's real width, expressed rather than guessed. A single vw
    figure cannot be right across the range: the left gutter is
    clamp(220px, 18.7vw, 300px), so below 1604px it scales with the viewport
    and above it is a fixed 300px — the column is 38vw of a 1440 screen but
    41vw of a 1920 one. A flat "40vw" therefore UNDER-states it on large
    screens, and understating `sizes` is what makes the browser pick too small
    a candidate, i.e. the blur this is meant to prevent. Over-stating only
    costs bytes, so both branches keep ~2% of headroom.

      >= 1604px : (100vw - 300 - 40 - 84) * 581/1108
      >=  750px : (100vw - 18.7vw - 40 - 5.3vw) * 581/1108
      <   750px : one column, 40px page margin each side
  endcomment
  assign pdp_media_sizes = '(min-width: 1604px) calc(53vw - 220px), (min-width: 750px) calc(41vw - 20px), calc(100vw - 80px)'

  comment
    HERO comes from the selected variant, the way Shopify means it to: the
    image attached to that variant in Admin, falling back to the product's
    own featured image. Arriving at ?variant=<black> therefore shows the
    black photograph before a single line of script runs.
  endcomment
  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign hero_media = current_variant.featured_media | default: product.featured_media | default: product_images.first

  comment
    An image with no alt of its own does not report an empty string: Liquid
    hands back the PRODUCT TITLE. Composing on top of that produced "Ball Boy
    Bowl — Ball Boy Bowl", so the title is treated as "nothing was written".
    It also means an unlabelled image can never match an option value, which
    is exactly right — it is shared.
  endcomment
  assign title_key = product.title | downcase | strip

  comment
    The hero carries a merchant-written alt too — usually just "Black" — so it
    gets the same composition as the gallery rather than announcing a bare
    colour name on its own.
  endcomment
  assign hero_alt_raw = hero_media.alt | default: '' | strip
  assign hero_alt_key = hero_alt_raw | downcase
  if hero_alt_key == title_key
    assign hero_alt_raw = ''
  endif
  if hero_alt_raw != blank
    assign hero_alt = product.title | append: ' — ' | append: hero_alt_raw
  else
    assign hero_alt = product.title
  endif

  comment
    GALLERY LABELS. Shopify attaches only ONE image per variant, so the rest
    of the gallery has no native way to say which colour it belongs to. The
    alt text carries it, and the whole alt IS the label: the merchant types
    "Black" and nothing else, matched case-insensitively after trimming.

    Accessibility is not paid for by that brevity — the alt that actually
    reaches a screen reader is composed here as "<product title> — <what was
    typed>", so "Black" renders as "Ball Boy Bowl — Black". The person
    labelling images never writes the product name; the page always states it.

    A label only counts when it matches a real option value of THIS product,
    which is why the vocabulary is built first. Anything else — "packaging",
    "scale reference", any plain description of the photo — is shared and
    shows on every variant, still with the product title composed in front.

    Delimiters on both sides (|black|) so "Black" cannot match "Blackberry".
  endcomment
  assign option_vocab = '|'
  unless product.has_only_default_variant
    for option in product.options_with_values
      for value in option.values
        assign option_vocab = option_vocab | append: value.name | downcase | append: '|'
      endfor
    endfor
  endunless

  comment
    THE LEAD PHOTOGRAPH (Eugenia, 2026-09-27). A product's image 2 is the one
    in context and image 1 the e-commerce shot on white; the page opens on
    image 2. Both are counted inside the set the variant filter leaves on
    screen, never in the product's raw list: the variant's own image, then
    every photograph the filter keeps, in product order. The second of that
    set leads in the hero, the first opens the gallery, the rest follow in
    their usual order. A set of one has nothing to promote and shows alone.

    Collection cards are untouched: their hover reads images 1 and 2 by
    position, straight from the product.

    It runs here, before any markup, because the hero is drawn first and has
    to know which photograph won. The gallery is captured now and printed
    further down; image 1 of the set is drawn last, once it is known whether
    anything was promoted over it (if not, it stays the hero and its gallery
    copy stays hidden).
  endcomment
  assign lead_media = hero_media
  assign lead_alt = hero_alt
  assign lead_found = false
  assign first_found = false
  assign gallery_first = ''
  assign gallery_rest = ''

  assign show_gallery = false
  if show_media and product_images.size > 1
    assign show_gallery = true
  endif

  if show_gallery
    assign filter_on = true
    if media_block.settings.gallery_filter == false
      assign filter_on = false
    endif

    for media in product_images
      comment
        The whole alt is the label. Trimmed and lower-cased so "  black " and
        "Black" both land on the same option value. Shopify falls back to the
        product title when an image has no alt of its own — see the note
        above. Treat that as unwritten.
      endcomment
      assign raw_alt = media.alt | default: '' | strip
      assign raw_alt_key = raw_alt | downcase
      if raw_alt_key == title_key
        assign raw_alt = ''
      endif
      assign label = ''
      if filter_on and raw_alt != blank
        assign probe = '|' | append: raw_alt | downcase | append: '|'
        if option_vocab contains probe
          assign label = raw_alt | downcase
        endif
      endif

      comment
        What a screen reader gets, composed rather than typed. An image with
        nothing written keeps just the product title instead of a dangling
        dash.
      endcomment
      if raw_alt != blank
        assign clean_alt = product.title | append: ' — ' | append: raw_alt
      else
        assign clean_alt = product.title
      endif

      comment
        Hidden server-side when the label belongs to another variant, so the
        page arrives already filtered and the browser never fetches those
        files (they are lazy AND display:none). The script only flips the
        same attribute when the shopper switches.
      endcomment
      assign hide = false
      if label != blank
        assign in_current = false
        for opt_value in current_variant.options
          assign opt_key = opt_value | downcase
          if opt_key == label
            assign in_current = true
          endif
        endfor
        unless in_current
          assign hide = true
        endunless
      endif

      comment
        Image 1 of the set is matched by IDENTITY, not by position: it is the
        selected variant's own image, which may sit anywhere in the list.
      endcomment
      if media.id == hero_media.id
        assign first_found = true
        assign first_index = forloop.index
        assign first_label = label
        assign first_alt = clean_alt
        continue
      endif

      comment
        Image 2 of the set: the first photograph after it that the filter
        keeps. It moves up to the hero, so its gallery copy is hidden.
      endcomment
      assign item_hidden = hide
      if lead_found == false and hide == false
        assign lead_found = true
        assign lead_media = media
        assign lead_alt = clean_alt
        assign item_hidden = true
      endif

      capture item
        render 'pdp-gallery-item', media: media, index: forloop.index, label: label, alt: clean_alt, hidden: item_hidden, sizes: pdp_media_sizes
      endcapture
      assign gallery_rest = gallery_rest | append: item
    endfor

    if first_found
      assign first_hidden = true
      if lead_found
        assign first_hidden = false
      endif
      capture gallery_first
        render 'pdp-gallery-item', media: hero_media, index: first_index, label: first_label, alt: first_alt, hidden: first_hidden, sizes: pdp_media_sizes
      endcapture
    endif
  endif
-%}

<section class="main-product" style="--media-ratio: {{ media_ratio }}; --pdp-gallery-gap: {{ gallery_gap }}px; --pdp-column-gap: {{ column_gap }}px;">
  <div class="main-product__grid">
    {%- if show_media -%}
      <div class="main-product__media" {{ media_block.shopify_attributes }}>
        {%- if lead_media -%}
          <div class="main-product__media-item main-product__media-item--hero">
            {{-
              lead_media
              | image_url: width: 2400
              | image_tag:
                widths: '550, 750, 1100, 1500, 2000, 2400',
                sizes: pdp_media_sizes,
                loading: 'eager',
                fetchpriority: 'high',
                alt: lead_alt
            -}}
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="main-product__media-item main-product__media-item--empty" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="main-product__info">
      {%- if has_structure -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- unless block.type == 'media' -%}
            {% render 'pdp-block', type: block.type, block: block, product: product, section: section %}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'pdp-block', type: 'breadcrumb', product: product, section: section %}
        {% render 'pdp-block', type: 'title', product: product, section: section %}
        {% render 'pdp-block', type: 'variant_picker', product: product, section: section %}
        {% render 'pdp-block', type: 'description', product: product, section: section %}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {% render 'pdp-block', type: 'accordion', block: block, product: product, section: section %}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {% render 'pdp-block', type: 'add_to_cart', product: product, section: section %}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Gallery: every photograph of the set but the one in the hero, full column
      width, height from the image's own aspect ratio. Nothing is ever cropped
      — editorial rule. It is a grid child rather than a child of the media
      column so the single column on mobile can put it AFTER the info panel:
      otherwise the title, price and add-to-cart sit below three full-bleed
      photos. On desktop it lands back under the hero in the left column. A
      single-image product renders no gallery at all (no empty state, no
      placeholder). Every image is in the markup, hidden when it is not in the
      set on screen, so a variant switch never has to fetch markup.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if show_gallery -%}
      <div class="pdp-gallery" data-pdp-gallery>
        {{- gallery_first -}}
        {{- gallery_rest -}}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product page",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_vendor",
      "label": "Show vendor",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_ratio",
      "label": "Image aspect ratio",
      "options": [
        { "value": "3/4", "label": "Portrait 3:4" },
        { "value": "4/5", "label": "Portrait 4:5" },
        { "value": "1/1", "label": "Square" }
      ],
      "default": "4/5",
      "info": "Applies to the hero image only — gallery images are never cropped"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "column_gap",
      "label": "Space between the images and the information",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 10,
      "info": "Where the two sit side by side (tablet and desktop)."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "breadcrumb", "name": "Breadcrumb", "limit": 1 },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "name": "Title",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "title_font",
          "label": "Typeface",
          "options": [
            { "value": "heading", "label": "Primary" },
            { "value": "body", "label": "Secondary" }
          ],
          "default": "heading"
        },
        {
          "type": "color",
          "id": "title_color",
          "label": "Colour",
          "info": "Empty uses the theme's"
        },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "spacing_bottom",
          "label": "Space below",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 80,
          "step": 2,
          "unit": "px",
          "default": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "show_subtitle",
          "label": "Show subtitle",
          "default": true
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "show_vendor",
          "label": "Show vendor",
          "default": true,
          "info": "Also needs the section's vendor setting on"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "variant_picker",
      "name": "Variant picker",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "spacing_top",
          "label": "Space above the swatches",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 80,
          "step": 2,
          "unit": "px",
          "default": 26,
          "info": "Between the title and the colour swatches on this page. The one in Theme settings → Product cards is a different place: the grid card."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "option_style",
          "label": "Size and other options",
          "options": [
            { "value": "buttons", "label": "Buttons" },
            { "value": "dropdown", "label": "Dropdown" }
          ],
          "default": "buttons",
          "info": "Colour always uses swatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "hide_single_colour",
          "label": "Hide the colour swatch when there is only one colour",
          "default": true,
          "info": "A single circle offers no choice. Products with two or more colours keep theirs. The colour is still named in Product Details."
        }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "description", "name": "Description", "limit": 1 },
    {
      "type": "media",
      "name": "Media",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "media_ratio",
          "label": "Hero image ratio",
          "options": [
            { "value": "3/4", "label": "Portrait 3:4" },
            { "value": "4/5", "label": "Portrait 4:5" },
            { "value": "1/1", "label": "Square" }
          ],
          "default": "3/4",
          "info": "The hero only. Gallery images below it are never cropped."
        },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "gallery_gap",
          "label": "Space between gallery images",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 64,
          "step": 2,
          "unit": "px",
          "default": 10,
          "info": "The air between the stacked photographs, and between the hero and the first of them"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "gallery_filter",
          "label": "Filter gallery by variant",
          "default": true,
          "info": "Shopify attaches only one image per variant, so label the rest through their alt text: type just the variant name, e.g. Black. Capitals and stray spaces don't matter. The alt a screen reader hears is written for you as \"Product name — Black\", so there is nothing else to type. An image whose alt isn't a variant name — packaging, a scale shot — shows on every variant."
        }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "add_to_cart", "name": "Add to cart", "limit": 1 },
    {
      "type": "product_details",
      "name": "Product details",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Product Details"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Details",
          "info": "Material, dimensions… Connect a product metafield (dynamic source) so each product shows its own lines."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "heading_font",
          "label": "Heading typeface",
          "options": [
            { "value": "body", "label": "Secondary" },
            { "value": "heading", "label": "Primary" }
          ],
          "default": "body"
        },
        {
          "type": "color",
          "id": "text_color",
          "label": "Text colour",
          "info": "Empty uses the theme's"
        },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "spacing_top",
          "label": "Space above",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 120,
          "step": 4,
          "unit": "px",
          "default": 56
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "show_color",
          "label": "Show the selected colour",
          "default": true,
          "info": "Follows the variant the shopper picks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "accordion",
      "name": "Accordion",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "Shipping & returns"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Content",
          "default": "<p>Share your shipping and returns policy here.</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 16,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Product page",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "media" },
        { "type": "breadcrumb" },
        { "type": "title" },
        { "type": "variant_picker" },
        { "type": "description" },
        { "type": "accordion" },
        { "type": "add_to_cart" },
        { "type": "product_details" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
